 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+
+## Cross-document view transitions
+
+The shared layout uses native document navigation and the global stylesheet opts
+all pages into view transitions, except when reduced motion is requested. Astro's
+bundled CSS and the font stylesheet load in the document head before rendering.
+
+Each page must include exactly one `id="initial-view"` on the last element of its
+initial content section. The layout's `rel="expect"` link waits until that element
+has been fully parsed, without waiting for below-the-fold articles or ads. Legal
+pages place this checkpoint at the end of their introduction.
+
+Initial content is server-rendered; React hydration adds interactivity without
+establishing the initial layout. If a new script is required to establish that
+layout (for example, applying a saved theme), place it in the head with
+`blocking="render"` so it loads and executes before the transition. Keep analytics,
+ads, and other noncritical scripts out of this render-blocking path. The parsing
+checkpoint does not wait for images to download or React islands to hydrate.
